{"reference":"1 Samuel 13","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":13,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Saul's Kingship","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Samuel treats Saul's offering as a failure to keep the command he had received, not merely as a mistake made under military pressure. The consequence is stated in terms of kingship: Saul's kingdom will not endure. The book later returns to this theme by contrasting sacrifice with obedience, so these verses introduce a decisive problem in Saul's rule.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 13:13-14"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_013_e320da1eea48bc9c9d280402"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Place in 1 Samuel","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"This chapter stands within a larger movement in 1 Samuel: the story moves from Eli's failing priestly house, through Samuel's leadership, to Saul's rejected kingship and then to David's rise. Saul's loss of an enduring dynasty here is therefore an important turning point in that larger narrative movement.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 1","1 Samuel 10:1-27","1 Samuel 11:1-15","1 Samuel 12:1-25","1 Samuel 14:1-52","1 Samuel 15:1-35","1 Samuel 16:1-23","1 Samuel 17:1-58","1 Samuel 18:1-30","1 Samuel 19:1-24","1 Samuel 20:1-42","1 Samuel 21:1-15","1 Samuel 22:1-23","1 Samuel 23:1-29","1 Samuel 24:1-22","1 Samuel 25:1-44","1 Samuel 26:1-25","1 Samuel 27:1-12","1 Samuel 28:1-25","1 Samuel 29:1-11","1 Samuel 2:1-36","1 Samuel 30:1-31","1 Samuel 31:1-13","1 Samuel 3:1-21","1 Samuel 4:1-22","1 Samuel 5:1-12","1 Samuel 6:1-21","1 Samuel 7:1-17","1 Samuel 8:1-22","1 Samuel 9:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_013_435c7a885f12694a4bbd832e"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}